WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.990
- You are so cute.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:02.943
- Thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:00:02.943 --> 00:00:03.776
Thank you.
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:03.776 --> 00:00:04.910
Congratulations on the Grammy noms.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:05.743
- Thank you very much.

00:00:05.743 --> 00:00:06.576
- That's very exciting.

00:00:06.576 --> 00:00:08.790
It is not about the awards
which is validating to know

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.550
that people are like
into what you're doing.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:11.670
- It is very validating.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.620
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.780
So your musical name is
Japanese Breakfast and I'm,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.920
please tell me that like
every time someone asks you,

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.090
why did you name that,

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.380
you make up a different story every time

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.213
'cause that would be really funny.

00:00:21.213 --> 00:00:24.237
- (laughs) Yeah, it doesn't
have the best story.

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:25.070
- Oh!

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.650
- I was in another band
that was very unpopular

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.653
and I had kind of this side project

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.992
that I was putting songs
up on Tumblr at the time.

00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:35.825
- Yeah.

00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:36.670
- And I just called it Japanese Breakfast

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.380
'cause I was weirdly following
all of these animated gifts

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.890
of Japanese Breakfast, and it
just seemed really appealing.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:43.832
And that's what I named

00:00:43.832 --> 00:00:44.665
the project.
- That's not a boring story.

00:00:44.665 --> 00:00:45.498
That's funny.

00:00:45.498 --> 00:00:46.331
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:46.331 --> 00:00:47.164
- It's something you liked.
- Yeah.

00:00:47.164 --> 00:00:48.840
- And it's something
that you don't forget.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.840
When you hear that name,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.100
like I will forever remember that title.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.160
- I feel like it makes people wonder

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.405
what exactly a Japanese
breakfast is, and it's--

00:00:55.405 --> 00:00:56.238
- And then, why do I
want one all a sudden.

00:00:56.238 --> 00:00:57.071
- Yes, yes.

00:00:57.071 --> 00:00:58.260
And then it's a very surprising

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.440
very appealing group of foods.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.355
- I'm into it.

00:01:01.355 --> 00:01:02.188
(Michelle laughs)

00:01:02.188 --> 00:01:04.730
Okay, so rumor has it that
you were with Doja Cat

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.670
when she was in the restroom
before when she was supposed

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.950
to be winning her award when she ran out.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.860
- I wasn't with her,
but I was like in the--

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:10.693
- Rumor has it

00:01:10.693 --> 00:01:12.397
you were peeing in the stall.
- In the bathroom.

00:01:12.397 --> 00:01:15.350
- No, that y'all were
in the restroom, sorry.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.820
- I had just like finished
peeing and she came in.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.150
And I was like, oh my God,
maybe I can like, hang out

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.490
and get a like bathroom
selfie with Doja Cat.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.380
And then I was kind of like,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.810
that's really weird to wait for her,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.259
like outside of the bathroom.

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:29.092
(audience laughing)
- Bathroom.

00:01:29.092 --> 00:01:31.490
- So then I was like, I'll
just go out into the hall

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.470
and try to get a snack and
wait for her to come out,

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.120
and then I'll get a photo with her.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:35.953
- Yeah.

00:01:35.953 --> 00:01:36.786
- And then someone--
- That's respectful.

00:01:36.786 --> 00:01:37.619
- Yes, yeah.

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:38.709
Give her her time and space.

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:39.542
- Yes.

00:01:39.542 --> 00:01:40.723
- And then someone came
running by and was like,

00:01:40.723 --> 00:01:41.980
"Doja Cat, Doja Cat, Doja Cat!"

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.460
And she ran into the bathroom

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:47.260
and then just started
pulling her out by the wrist

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.160
to go back in.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.120
And they had all of us in the holding

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.460
'cause the commercial break was over

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.350
and she had just won her Grammy.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.080
And so she like, they like flew her in,

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.553
her dress flew up and
exposed her (laughs).

00:01:57.553 --> 00:01:58.850
- Everything.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.290
- Yeah, and then I found out
later that she won the Grammy

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.742
but I was like in holding--

00:02:02.742 --> 00:02:03.575
- You didn't gey your pictures.

00:02:03.575 --> 00:02:04.590
- I didn't get my picture.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.550
She got her Grammy though.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.300
- See now, that was the sad story.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.140
That wasn't about the Japanese Breakfast.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:09.973
That's sad.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.973 --> 00:02:10.806
- You're gonna get it.

00:02:10.806 --> 00:02:11.639
- And I'm proud of her.

00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:12.472
- We're gonna make this happen.

00:02:12.472 --> 00:02:13.305
Oh my gosh, me too.

00:02:13.305 --> 00:02:14.138
I love her.
- A big fan, yeah.

00:02:14.138 --> 00:02:15.030
- Yeah, she's very talented.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.060
And if anybody's gonna be
showing anybody, she is amazing.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.400
I'm like, wow, you work
hard for that ma'am.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.680
So your memoir is called
"Crying in H Mart."

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.837
So it's about your mom, right?

00:02:23.837 --> 00:02:24.670
- Yeah.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.670
And is H Mart a place obviously?

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.180
- Yeah, so despite the
name Japanese Breakfast,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.210
my mom was Korean and so
I'm half Korean, half white.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.140
And H Mart is a supermarket chain

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.540
known for selling Korean groceries.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:38.373
- Yeah.

00:02:38.373 --> 00:02:41.830
- And so in 2014, unfortunately
my mom passed away of cancer

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.470
and I lived in Eugene for
six months as a caretaker

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.939
when she was going through chemotherapy.

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:46.772
- Yeah.

00:02:46.772 --> 00:02:48.140
- So the book kind of
documents that process.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.420
And part of my grieving
process sort of landed

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.760
on learning how to cook Korean dishes.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.450
And so every time I went to
this Korean grocery store,

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.250
H Mart, I would see like
a package of seaweed

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.760
and I would be like, well,
I can't call my mom anymore

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.760
to ask what brand of
seaweed we used to buy.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.870
- Oh!
- Or I would see like,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.200
a can of sweet red beans,
and I would remember

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.350
we'd used to have this shaved
ice dessert in the summers

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.970
every time we visited Seoul and so,

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.260
I would cry in H Mart.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.740
And the book is about learning
how to cook Korean dishes

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.410
and kind of preserve
that part of my culture

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.365
after she passed away.

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:22.285
(audience applauding)
- That's really cool.

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:24.296
And then she's still kinda with you.

00:03:24.296 --> 00:03:25.254
- Yeah, I mean--

00:03:25.254 --> 00:03:26.087
- I think that's beautiful.

00:03:26.087 --> 00:03:26.920
- Yes, it is.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:27.753
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:27.753 --> 00:03:28.586
- That she's still kind
of with you in that sense.

00:03:28.586 --> 00:03:29.419
That's awesome.

00:03:29.419 --> 00:03:30.252
- Yeah.

00:03:30.252 --> 00:03:32.440
- So you're performing
your song, it's "Be Sweet,"

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.940
and that's up next and
I'm very excited about.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.170
So what's the song about,
other than you should be sweet?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.680
- Yeah, I mean, in simple terms

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.959
it's basically please just be nice to me.

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:41.270
(both laughing)
- Yeah.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.500
- I wrote that song in 2018
with someone named Jack Tatum

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.240
who plays in a band called Wild Nothing.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.050
So we got together in his
studio and we were like,

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.810
well I guess like, we
should just write a pop song

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.750
and like try to sell
it to like a pop star.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.583
- Yeah.

00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:53.416
- Like Kelly Clarkson or something.

00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:54.249
- Okay.

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:56.920
- And then I just liked
it so much that I kept it,

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.350
and I feel like it's a
very, it's like a diva bomb.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:01.190
- That worked out.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.023
- Yes, it worked out.

00:04:02.023 --> 00:04:02.856
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:04:02.856 --> 00:04:04.000
- Well, once again, Michelle's book

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.530
is called "Crying in H Mart."

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.789
You gotta check it out, it's
40 weeks, congratulations.

00:04:07.789 --> 00:04:08.622
- Thank you.

00:04:08.622 --> 00:04:10.053
- New York Times best
seller, that's amazing.

